<title>AUSTRALIA: NSW state shows A$151 mln underlying surplus.</title>
<headline>NSW state shows A$151 mln underlying surplus.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New South Wales (NSW) state Treasury said on Monday the underlying financial result for the NSW budget sector for the six months to December 1996 is a surplus of A$151 million.</p>
<p>This compares to a surplus of A$163 million for the same period last year and a A$185 million deficit for the five months to November 1996.</p>
<p>--Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
